            "text": "ABOUT THE WRITING"
          }
        },
        "richtext_8KGtUw": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "paragraph_class_name": "richtext-p-section",
            "content": "<p><em><strong>Make It Make Sense </strong></em>is where I think out loud. Some pieces are about the mental health field, what is broken in it, what is shifting, and what clinicians and clients should know. Some are clinical writing on diagnosis and practice. Some are reflections on what is happening in the world, read through a psychological lens. And some are practical, about the stress of daily life and how to move through it.</p><p>I write for clinicians, helping professionals, graduate students, and thoughtful readers who want clinical depth without jargon. The pieces are research-informed and clinically grounded, but they are written in my voice, with my words. An attempt to make sense of the work, the world, and the work of being an imperfect person, in public.</p>"
          }
        }
